#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Phase 432 in CLAUDE.md: the Phase row.   python3 claudemd432.py <CLAUDE.md>
import sys
p = sys.argv[1]; s = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()
if '| 432 | 2026-10-12 |' in s: raise SystemExit('CLAUDE.md: row 432 already there')
row = """| 432 | 2026-10-12 | **Chapter 7 (Tones & Semitones) started: Lesson Book draft v1 + review pack.** After her 06:38 'and let's go on to the next one'. Built on her own lesson words (a semitone is your BEST FRIEND -- the very next key, nobody in between; a tone is a FRIEND OF A FRIEND -- one key in between; Korean 베프 / 친구의 친구, 반음 / 온음), chapter 2's keyboard street (small house, big house), chapter 3's residents, the bird's sky / turtle's sea, chapter 6's 'the same key, two ways'. AMEB checked (2026 Manual): Music Craft Prelim -- recognise and write the sharp and flat; Grade 1 -- sharp, flat and natural, the concepts enharmonic and chromatic, tones/semitones marked on scales; Theory Grade 1 -- sharp, flat, natural, tones and semitones in C, G, F major; double sharps/flats Grade 4 (both); Piano for Leisure Grade 1 technical work: chromatic scale hands separately. Draft 7 pages (_workspace/chapter-review/g432/x/tn432.jsx + apply432.py; a draft build only, drills.src.html unchanged): 1 Clara at her C with her two best friends (B and the black key on her right, coral hearts) and two friends of a friend (outline hearts); 2 Best friends: a semitone (the Dog's two are black keys; a black key's two are white keys; the best-friend walk C to C = 12 semitones); 3 A friend of a friend: a tone (C to D over the black key; black to black over one white key; two hops = one tone; set pairs to play); 4 White best friends: E F and B C (the Exit and the Front door; the Back door and Clara; tone tone semitone tone tone tone semitone); 5 Sharp and flat: one key, two names (the sharp sign up to the best friend on the right, the flat sign down to the left; every black key named both ways); 6 Sharps and flats on the staff (just before the note on its line or space; 4 in Queensland, 4 in Kingsland); 7 My five checks. Signs in text use the music font at 1.5x (tnSign); staff signs are drawn (tnAcc). A fresh-eyes reviewer checked every key, name, heart, arrow and staff position en+ko (all music right); its fixes are in (the sharp sign not 'A sharp', Korean ♯는, the natural taken out until bar lines -- B6, set pairs, 'almost every key', 'the other best friend', 'count the steps, not the keys', layout). Review pack Claude outputs/Chapter-07-review-v1-Tones-Semitones.pdf (12 pages): G1-G3 guide questions with suggestions; A1-A8 on today's chapter 7 (not the book on screen; double sharps and the written chromatic scale (Grade 4-5) in a Preliminary chapter, E♯ = F; 'an accidental lasts until the bar line' before bar lines; half/whole step; the drill's levels; the Phase 298 Workbook/Teacher copy; the map room says 'Sharps & flats'; the double dash '--' breaking across lines in every book); B1-B11 with recommendations (words, Clara as 'you', the residents for E F / B C, one key two names, how to remember the signs (a) direction only, the natural waits for bar lines, what waits for later, the best-friend walk = chromatic in the Teacher copy only, 7 drill levels, Workbook W1-W5, minimal opener). Checks: lbcheck tones 0 overflow en/ko. Phase 431 the same day: chapter 6 after her notes on v2. |
"""
i = s.index('| 431 | 2026-10-12 |'); j = s.index('\n', i) + 1
s = s[:j] + row + s[j:]
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s); print('CLAUDE.md ok')
